# `s = s + data[w][i]; data[w][i] = data[w][i] + 2`, holder and key parameters of which nobody knows anything. A loop that stores by key once asked for no row: every copy by member read generically behind the store.
# A store into an element of the row itself lays nothing under a name of the holder. Where what is stored is a number as soon as the row holds numbers, the row is asked for; the look for lists takes `data[w]` for the row
# that was found in front, as it takes `const r = data[w]`: it is tested, its storage is converted and it is stored into by the typed form. The conversion writes shape words, so the row is read once more behind it, by the
# operation that runs no code, and held against the row in front: in front of the typed copy, for no turn writes what that read reads. 70,025 > 3,057 instructions three hundred turns (by hand 2,690, plain Bun 3,980).
